Title:
Red Clippy

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- Red Clippy is an open-source pentest management platform designed to be operated by an AI coding agent via MCP (Model Context Protocol), while keeping a durable engagement record.  
- It addresses the common failure mode of agent-driven testing where context is lost between sessions, leading to repeated scans, missed coverage tracking, and “forgotten” confirmed findings.  
- The tool provides a web UI + REST API + an MCP JSON-RPC stdio server so an agent can create/maintain scope, assets, observations, methodology check coverage, findings (with CVSS/CWE/CVE), and evidence uploads.  
- It includes tool-output ingestion with parsers/auto-detection for common scanners (e.g., nmap, Burp, Nessus, OpenVAS, masscan, naabu, subfinder) and stores results transactionally.  
- It also supports an attack graph for linking nodes/relations and computing paths, plus multi-tenant org separation for consultants handling multiple clients.  
- Useful primarily for red teams/pentesters experimenting with agent-assisted workflows, and for blue/purple teams reviewing structured evidence and repeatable methodology coverage.

Technical Focus:
- MCP integration (JSON-RPC 2.0 stdio) for agent-driven operations
- Pentest data model: orgs, engagements, assets vs observations, findings, evidence
- Methodology coverage tracking mapped to OWASP WSTG (built-in checks)
- Scanner output ingestion/parsing (nmap, Burp, Nessus, OpenVAS, masscan, naabu, subfinder)
- REST API with org-scoped bearer keys; local-first deployment (127.0.0.1)
- Attack graph modeling and shortest-path traversal

Use Cases:
- Run an AI-assisted engagement while preserving scope, coverage, and evidence across sessions
- Ingest scanner outputs into a structured engagement record for triage and reporting
- Track methodology/checklist completion per asset to avoid re-testing cleared ground
- Maintain multi-client separation (organizations) for consulting workflows
- Build and analyze attack paths using a lightweight engagement attack graph

Keywords:
Red Clippy, MCP, Model Context Protocol, JSON-RPC 2.0, pentest management, AI agent, Claude Code, OpenAI Codex CLI, REST API, SQLite, OWASP WSTG, methodology coverage, CVSS 3.1, CWE, CVE, evidence management, nmap, Burp Suite, Nessus, OpenVAS, masscan, naabu, subfinder, attack graph